      "seconds_since_start": 0.082,
      "seconds_since_previous_block": 0.082
    },
    "text": "I can look into this \u2014 Lake Formation permission issues like this usually come down to the IAM role used by EMR (or its EC2 instance profile) not having the right Lake Formation grants on the specific database/table.\n\nTo check this properly, I'll need a few specifics:\n\n1. **Which database and table** is the Spark job trying to read?\n2. **Which IAM role** is the EMR job using (the EC2 instance profile role, or if this is an EMR Studio/Notebook runtime role, that one)?\n3. **Which AWS account and region** is this in?\n4. Any error message/log snippet you have from the Spark job (helps confirm exactly which permission \u2014 SELECT, DESCRIBE, data filters \u2014 is missing)?\n\nIf you can give me the role name and the database/table, I'll check the current Lake Formation grants and data lake settings to pinpoint what's missing."
  },
